"imported yet, but it can also mean the file was changed."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:106
msgid ""
"Do not go on until you know why. Import the vendor's key only after checking "
"its fingerprint on the official web site."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:109
msgid "A signing key has expired"
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:110
msgid ""
"The key that guarantees a repository is out of date, so nothing from that "
"repository can be installed or updated until the key is renewed."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:112
msgid ""
"Usually the vendor publishes a renewed key: import it (Signing keys → Import "
"a key…)."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:114
msgid "Some open programs still use the old version"
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:115
msgid ""
"Programs that were open during the update keep using the old files until "
"they are closed. Nothing is broken."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:117
msgid ""
"Close and reopen them when it suits you. Restart the computer only if Zypp "
"Desk says so."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:120
msgid "zypper asked a question that nobody could answer"
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:121
msgid ""
"zypper stopped to ask (for example “Continue?”), but it was not running in a "
"terminal, so it could not read an answer and gave up. Nothing was changed by "
"that command."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:123
msgid ""
"Run it again: Zypp Desk now adds -n so that zypper takes its default answers."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:126
msgid "Reminder before a distribution upgrade"
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:127
msgid ""
"zypper always says this before 'dup': it will use every enabled repository, "
"so they should all be meant for your version of the system."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:129
msgid "Nothing, if your repositories are the usual ones."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:131
msgid "Some packages were not checked for file conflicts"
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:132
msgid ""
"In a simulation the packages are not downloaded, so zypper cannot look "
"inside them. The real installation does check them."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:136
msgid "Another program is using the package manager"
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:137
msgid ""
"Only one program at a time can use zypper. It may be Zypp Desk's own refresh "
"in the background (a timer refreshes the repositories every six hours), or "
"zypper in a terminal."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:139
msgid ""
"Wait a moment and try again. At the bottom left, Zypp Desk says which "
"program is using it."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:141
msgid ""
"The server of a repository (one of its mirrors) does not have a file that "
"the repository's list on your computer names. Usually that mirror is still "
"copying a new version, or your list is older than the server's."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:144
msgid ""
"Refresh the repositories and try again. If it keeps happening with the same "
"repository, its address may have changed (Repositories → ✎ Address…)."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:149
msgid "A repository did not answer"
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:150
msgid ""
"The server of a repository did not respond, or there is no Internet "
"connection. zypper uses what it already knew about that repository."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:152
msgid ""
"Try again later. If it happens every time, that repository may no longer "
"exist: disable it in Repositories."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:157
msgid "A dependency problem"
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:158
msgid ""
"What you asked for needs something that is missing, or clashes with "
"something you have. zypper stops so it does not break anything."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:160
msgid ""
"Look at the simulation: change the queue (lock or remove the package that "
"clashes) and simulate again."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:163
msgid "A package's install script failed"
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:164
msgid ""
"The package was installed, but the small program that sets it up afterwards "
"reported an error. Sometimes it does not matter; sometimes something stays "
"unconfigured."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:166
msgid "If the program does not work well, reinstall that package."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:170
msgid "Restart the computer"
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:171
msgid ""
"An update changed something basic (for example the kernel or the system "
"libraries) that only takes effect after a restart."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:173
msgid "Restart when it suits you."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:175
msgid "Checked without administrator rights"
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:176
msgid ""
"This check ran as your user, so it could only look at your own programs."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:179
msgid "Something no longer gets updates"
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:180
msgid ""
"A Flatpak runtime or app has reached its end of life: it will not get "
"security fixes any more."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:181
msgid ""
"Update the app; if it keeps using it, look for a newer version or an "
"alternative."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:185
msgid "Two packages want the same file"
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:186
msgid ""
"Two packages contain a file with the same name. Installing both could "
"overwrite one with the other."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:188
msgid ""
"Usually one of them comes from an extra repository: choose one of the two."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:245
msgid "A message Zypp Desk does not know yet"
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:246
msgid ""
"zypper (or a package) wrote this and Zypp Desk has no explanation for it. It "
"is not necessarily bad: many messages are only informative."
msgstr ""

#: zypp_desk/explain.py:248
msgid ""
"If something does not work afterwards, search for the exact text on the "
"Internet."
msgstr ""

